{
  "esm": "2.1.0",
  "metadata": {
    "name": "str_csig",
    "description": "Scalar atom of the CICE stress-combination algebra (ice_dyn_evp.F90:1667-1686, the csigp*/csigm*/csig12* corner averages): csig = c1*a1 + c2*(a2 + a4) + c3*a3. Each csig term of the Fortran is p111 times one corner value plus p055/p111 times the opposite-corner pair plus p027/p055 times the third corner; e.g. csigpne = p111*p1 + p055*(p2 + p4) + p027*p3 (F90:1667) binds a1 = p1, a2 = p2, a3 = p3, a4 = p4, c1 = p111, c2 = p055, c3 = p027, and csig12ne = p222*s1 + p111*(s2 + s4) + p055*s3 (F90:1683) binds c1 = p222, c2 = p111, c3 = p055. Pure combination algebra: no faq, no index sets of its own.",
    "license": "MIT",
    "tags": ["esd:stencil", "family:cice_bgrid", "grid:cice_bgrid", "op:stress"],
    "references": [
      {
        "citation": "Hunke, E. C., et al. (2023). CICE v6.3.22 documentation and user's guide (LA-UR-23-31851), the stress() corner combinations."
      }
    ]
  },
  "expression_templates": {
    "str_csig": {
      "params": ["a1", "a2", "a3", "a4", "c1", "c2", "c3"],
      "body": {
        "op": "+",
        "args": [
          { "op": "*", "args": ["c1", "a1"] },
          { "op": "*", "args": ["c2", { "op": "+", "args": ["a2", "a4"] }] },
          { "op": "*", "args": ["c3", "a3"] }
        ]
      }
    }
  }
}
